WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.090
Mumbai.

2
00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:08.130
About 20.2 million people, crowded at
about 27,000 people per square kilometre.

3
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:14.090
It is an Alpha world city, and the home
of India's central bank since 1937.

4
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:19.010
On the city's edge lies M East,
one of Mumbai's municipal wards.

5
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:23.370
Since the 1960s, it has taken
in migrants from across India.

6
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.290
You may live thousands of miles away.

7
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.550
So how do you study a place like this?

8
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.650
Can you, without going there?

9
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.730
In this mission, you'll profile the ward,

10
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.030
and trace the flows of people,
money and ideas that shape it.

11
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.350
Then you'll set it beside
a London neighbourhood,

12
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.390
and compare two very different places.

13
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.760
Your mission: find out how to study
a place thousands of miles away.
